Chapter: AnnotationQueryTest
  cites Works chapter Annotation
  cites Works chapter AnnotationsQuery
  cites Works chapter AnnotationsSidecar
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 The side query, against the real thing. The fixture below is the verbatim
 content of `annotations/codex/Emit/PeWriter.json` as it sits in the depot,
 not a shape invented to suit the parser. That is the point: the sidecar
 format is a claim made in `annotations/README.md`, the parser is a separate
 claim in `AnnotationsSidecar`, and nothing had ever put the two together.
 One of the five depot sidecars is a bare object where the README specifies
 an array, which no reader would have survived and no test could have seen.

 The path assertion is here for the same reason. `sidecar-path-for` built
 `codex.annotations/...` while the directory on disk has always been
 `annotations/`, and the only caller was a test supplying its own fixture,
 so the two never met.

Section: Fixture

  aqt-json : Text
  aqt-json = "[{\"target\": \"function:pe-uefi-stub\", \"kind\": \"rationale\", \"author\": \"cam\", \"date\": \"2026-05-06\", \"body\": \"Stub is self-measuring.\", \"thread\": null}, {\"target\": \"function:pe-scan-hlt\", \"kind\": \"warning\", \"author\": \"cam\", \"date\": \"2026-05-06\", \"body\": \"Pattern breaks silently if the tick address moves.\", \"thread\": null}]"

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    let xs = annq-parse "Emit/PeWriter" aqt-json
    in let warns = annq-by-kind xs "warning"
    in let byt = annq-by-target xs "function:pe-uefi-stub"
    in act
      print-line-uni ("parsed=" & show (annq-count xs))
      print-line-uni ("warning=" & show (annq-count-of-kind xs "warning"))
      print-line-uni ("rationale=" & show (annq-count-of-kind xs "rationale"))
      print-line-uni ("bytarget=" & show (list-length byt))
      print-line-uni ("path=" & sidecar-path-for "codex" "Emit/PeWriter")
      print-line-uni (annq-render warns)
    end
  end

